  "notes": [
    "All speed variants and repetitions of a route remain in its assigned split.",
    "Training sees rectangles and triangles; validation sees new zigzags; test sees irregular polygons. This is a small route-family generalization pilot, not an IID accuracy estimate.",
    "Do not use route waypoints or future connection states as model features.",
    "Observed speed is endpoint displacement divided by elapsed time; heading is previous-to-current bearing.",
    "Split before constructing windows. Fit scaling and any imputation only on training data.",
    "8 samples at 60-second intervals span 7 minutes. Target is 60 seconds after the last input.",
    "4356 raw rows is an estimate (36 x 121), not an observed result or an independent sample count.",
    "Fixed seed makes runs reproducible; changing only the seed is not a new route.",
    "Test configurations may be checked for mechanical validity and data integrity, but prediction quality must not guide route selection or tuning.",
    "Any failed run must be retained in the batch log. Do not silently drop it; repair infrastructure and rerun the same configuration or explicitly version the plan."
  ]
}
